# UBSan suppressions for the loader fuzz target (UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...).
# Only checks that the WAMR build makes recoverable (fuzz/build.sh) can be
# suppressed; everything else aborts.  Each entry is a known WAMR 2.4.5
# report, documented in doc/security.md (residual risks) with its
# reproducer under fuzz/loader/findings/:
#
# memory_instantiate (core/iwasm/interpreter/wasm_runtime.c:453):
#   memory->heap_data = memory->memory_data + heap_offset with memory_data
#   NULL for a linear memory of 0 pages ("applying zero offset to null
#   pointer").  NULL + 0, formally undefined in C, is a no-op with GCC and
#   Clang; nothing dereferences it (every access is bounds-checked against
#   a size of 0).  findings/wamr-null-plus-zero.wasm
pointer-overflow:memory_instantiate
